# candidate (a)).  Only THREE of the pre-LLM slot's four out-of-deadline
# overheads apply post-loop: measure + store + register.  The RESET term
# (restart + pristine reopen, RECIPE_PASS_RESET_RESERVE_S) is deliberately
# ABSENT — post-loop there is no LLM loop to hand a pristine session to,
# and the finalize path that follows is disk-truth-driven (every branch
# that needs Vivado re-opens the artifact it is about to touch itself;
# see the session-state audit comment in _run_recipe_pass_postloop_inner).
# Charging the 1800 s ship-scale reset reserve here would re-create the
# exact MAJOR-1 dead-code failure this slot exists to fix.
RECIPE_PASS_POSTLOOP_OVERHEAD_RESERVE_S = (
    RECIPE_PASS_MEASURE_RESERVE_S + RECIPE_PASS_STORE_RESERVE_S
    + RECIPE_PASS_REGISTER_RESERVE_S
)  # = 540.0
# ---- FPL26_RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP (aug04, DEFAULT OFF) --------------------------
# REVIEW_V30 MAJOR-1 lineage, third slot design: the PRE-LLM deep gate is
# UNARMABLE AS BUILT (1350 + 900 + 2400 = 4650s > 3200s max remaining) and
# the post-loop slot's residual firing set measured EMPTY at ship wall
# (aug03 night A/B: 0/7 fires — handback_armed x3, wall x2).  This variant
# makes the PRE-LLM deep gate armable via MEASURED-SIZE arithmetic instead
# of band-constant arithmetic.  Opt-in on top of the master flag: BOTH
# FPL26_RECIPE_PASS and FPL26_RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP must be truthy;
# FPL26_NO_RECIPE_PASS kills both.  Flag-off is byte-identical to the
# 12005bd deep gate.
#
# COST MODEL (no name keys — measured characteristics only):
#   predicted_recipe_cost = RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP_COST_RATIO x size_anchor,
#   where size_anchor is the SAME per-run size-model figure deep-replace
#   [first] uses (predict_place_route_s: primitive cells x 0.00435 s/cell).
#   Calibration (aug04 DEBUG-WALL box6 8c parity, end-to-end fire): vtr_v2
#   deep recipe measured 852s vs size anchor 343s -> ratio 852/343 = 2.48
#   ~= 2.5.  The 852s is the pass's own "result ... dt=" span: pristine
#   preopen -> 8 frozen steps (incl. the mid-recipe session round-trip) ->
#   measure -> store -> register.
RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP_COST_RATIO = 2.5
# Margin x1.2, NOT the 1.5 used for unmeasured recipes
# (RECIPE_PASS_TIMEOUT_FACTOR): the deep recipe is deterministic frozen
# Tcl with a MEASURED end-to-end cost on this exact step list (852s, one
# calibration point, byte-exact recipe) — 1.5x is the convention for
# costs that were never measured; a measured deterministic pass gets the
# tighter deterministic margin.  The hard per-pass timeout stays at
# 1.5x expected (unchanged) — this constant only sizes the FIRE GATE.
RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP_MARGIN = 1.2
# OVERHEAD AUDIT (the honest recompute the spec demanded): charging the
# full RECIPE_PASS_OVERHEAD_RESERVE_S (900s) on top of the margined
# prediction gives need = 1.2x(2.5x343) + 900 + 1100 ~= 3029s vs measured
# warm remaining ~2726s — DOES NOT FIT vtr, and bending the ratio/margin
# to force it would be tuning a constant to one design's record (house
# rule violation).  The fit comes from an AUDIT, not a tune: the 2.5
# calibration span (dt=852s, see above) ALREADY CONTAINS measure + store
# + register — those three reserves (120+180+240 = 540s) are INSIDE the
# measured cost the ratio was fitted to, and charging them again is the
# double-reserve defect class (project_double_reserve_defect_jul30).  The
# ONE overhead genuinely OUTSIDE the dt span is the post-pass reset
# (_recipe_pass_reset_session: restart + pristine reopen before the LLM
# loop, RECIPE_PASS_RESET_RESERVE_S = 360s) — the pre-LLM slot still
# needs it (there IS an LLM loop to hand a pristine session to; do not
# copy the post-loop 540 rationale), so it is the only reserve added.
#
# WORKED EXAMPLES (gate: need = 1.2 x (2.5 x anchor) + 360 + 1100):
#   vtr_v2 warm: 78,885 cells -> anchor 343s -> predicted 858s ->
#     need = 1029 + 360 + 1100 = 2489s vs remaining ~2726s -> FITS
#     (~237s headroom).
#   vtr_v2 cold: cold open costs ~405s vs 18s warm (aug04 cold-cache
#     forensics) -> remaining ~2339s < 2489s -> fail-closed skip.  The
#     gate firing warm-only is disclosed, not hidden (open risk #1 in
#     PANEL_PACK_aug04 — the A/B decides if that is value or noise).
#   boom_soc_v2 self-excludes BY ARITHMETIC, no name check: 379,380
#     cells -> anchor 1650s -> predicted 4126s -> need = 4951 + 360 +
#     1100 = 6411s > 3200s (the most any 1h wall can have remaining) —
#     never arms, matching the negative-control requirement (boom is
#     deep-replace-B2-dominated; the recipe adds ~nothing there).
#
# THE TRADE (reduced-tail bet, previously REJECTED — now measured): the
# 12005bd deep gate reserves the FULL deep-WNS tail (2400s) on top of the
# pass, which is what makes it dead code.  Here the tail-reserve term is
# REPLACED by the LLM floor (phys_opt_preempt_budget_floor_s, 1100s) —
# NOT added — and when the recipe banks a candidate the run's remaining
# tail reserve is explicitly REDUCED (see
# _recipe_first_deep_apply_reduced_tail).  REVIEW_V30 MAJOR-1 candidate
# (b) rejected exactly this bet BLIND ("a recipe miss eats the deep tail
# on the way down = the fence failure mode").  What changed: the bet is
# now MEASURED — the deterministic deep recipe banks 5.15 (vtr record
# class, byte-exact cross-box) while n=13 tail/loop outcomes on the same
# design never exceeded 4.14; and on a recipe MISS (fired, nothing
# banked) the tail reserve is left UNTOUCHED, so the miss path keeps the
# full deterministic tail — the fence failure mode is the guarded case,
# not the accepted one.
#
# HARDENING (aug04, external seat round 2 — adv_review_qwen_deep_aug04.md
# conditional-GO conditions).  All three protect UNKNOWN deep designs
# (user directive: generalizable gates, no per-design tuning); the vtr
# worked example is UNCHANGED by all three (re-derived below).
#
# (1) DYNAMIC ABORT (review Q2a/Q3): the 2.5 ratio is calibrated on ONE
# (852, 343) pair — the uncertainty is in the ratio GENERALIZING, not in
# vtr's own deterministic runtime (+-5%).  If recipe elapsed exceeds
# 0.75 x the fire-time need budget, the pass aborts between steps and
# reverts to pristine via the existing failure path — converting the
# unknown-design tail risk from "LLM starvation" to "wasted wall,
# pristine state".  Static 1.2 margin + 0.75 abort = effective 1.6x
# (1.2/0.75) overrun protection while preserving vtr's fit (the review's
# "defensible middle" between 1.2x and k3's 1.5x).  Rides the existing
# per-step deadline fencing (checked between steps, no new machinery).
# MAJOR-3 shape (adversarial review aug04): the effective cap is
#   min(0.75 x need, remaining_at_fire - gate LLM floor - reset 360s)
# — the second term guarantees a low-slack fire can never eat the LLM
# floor the gate promised.  On vtr that term GOVERNS: min(0.75 x 2489
# = 1867s, 2726 - 1100 - 360 = 1266s) = 1266s, tighter than the 1350s
# per-step fence — the abort is live on vtr, and the measured 852s
# (+-5%) recipe stays ~414s clear, so the zero-abort ship criterion
# still holds by arithmetic.  MAJOR-1 (same review) closes the
# companion hole at the gate itself: a margined prediction above the
# 1350s band-constant deadline (anchor > 450s; the wall-armable-yet-
# deadline-doomed anchor ~450-573s window) is skipped as
# deadline-unfundable instead of fired-then-fenced.
RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP_DYNAMIC_ABORT_FRAC = 0.75
# (2) SCALED LLM FLOOR (review Q2b): a fixed 1100s floor under-protects
# an unknown design with LARGE remaining — the gate could fire and leave
# the loop a floor sized for a smaller run.  floor = max(1100,
# 0.35 x remaining_at_gate): vtr unchanged (0.35 x 2726 = 954 < 1100);
# a hypothetical 4000s-remaining design gets 1400s, damping
# over-aggressive fires.  The reduced-tail step honors the SAME gate
# floor (stored at fire time) so the loop keeps what the gate promised.
RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP_LLM_FLOOR_FRAC = 0.35
# (3) ANCHOR FLOOR (review Q2c — the real danger): a pathological
# small-cell design routes 3-5x worse than the size model predicts, and
# a tiny anchor makes need trivial (5k cells -> anchor 22s -> need
# ~1526s fires trivially while the recipe could burn ~3000s).  Clamp
# the anchor to >= 100s inside THIS gate's arithmetic (predicted >=
# 300s, need >= ~1820s at the base floor) — conservative below
# ~23k cells (100/0.00435), where the deep recipe is unlikely to help
# anyway.  vtr unaffected (343 > 100).  The clamp is gate-local: the
# size model itself and deep-replace's use of it are untouched.
RECIPE_FIRST_DEEP_ANCHOR_FLOOR_S = 100.0


